== the help documents the forms and $KOSHCONF:
DESCRIPTION
  The koshconf builtin loads and changes the settings Koshka owns, writes the
  configuration file, and loads the binary form of KOSHCONF. save prints the
  current settings as the value of $KOSHCONF, which a child kosh adopts, and
  with --persist writes them to the user configuration file.

SYNOPSIS
  koshconf create <bash|sh|kosh> [--force]
  koshconf set <option> <value> [--persist]
  koshconf get <option>
  koshconf list [-a|--all]
  koshconf load <base64>
  koshconf save [--persist]

OPTIONS
      --help                            Display help.
  -a, --all                             With list, also show the legacy.posix
                                        and legacy.bash name of each option.
      --persist                         With set, also write the option to the
                                        user configuration file. With save,
                                        write every current setting to it.
      --force                           With create, replace an existing
                                        configuration file.
